{
  "where_we_lag": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "Keski-Suomi lags nationally in crude recorded multidisciplinary team meetings at 3.8% (95% CI 2.5–5.5; n=24/637) versus 6.0% (893/14873), and its regional pathway document lacks referral time limits.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "cty:mdt_recorded:Keski_Suomen_hyvinvointialue",
        "nat:mdt_recorded",
        "reg:ks_referral"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "The county's crude recorded MDT share of 3.8% (95% CI 2.5–5.5; n=24/637) has a 95% confidence interval that excludes the national 6.0% (893/14873), even though Keski-Suomi's regional pathway document states every new case is reviewed in an MDT, because HILMO records only direct patient contacts and measures recording practice rather than care.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Keski_Suomen_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:mdt_recorded",
          "reg:mdt_practice",
          "bs:coverage:MDT",
          "q:39e6ba43a9"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Across overlapping treatment categories, crude county shares include the national value within their 95% confidence intervals for curative care at 27.2% (95% CI 23.9–30.7; n=173/637) versus 27.0% (4009/14873) and symptomatic care at 36.3% (95% CI 32.6–40.1; n=231/637) versus 39.5% (5871/14873), whereas crude life-prolonging care at 37.2% (95% CI 33.5–41.0; n=237/637) excludes the national 30.4% (4522/14873).",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:curative:Keski_Suomen_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:curative",
          "cty:symptomatic:Keski_Suomen_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:symptomatic",
          "cty:life_prolonging:Keski_Suomen_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:life_prolonging"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Keski-Suomi's regional pathway document targets a lung clinic appointment within 2–3 weeks or at latest about 1 month and tissue sample results in about 1–2 weeks, but it states referrals are handled as quickly as possible without a time limit, names no diagnostic contact person, and does not report whether target times are met.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "reg:ks_target",
          "reg:ks_tissue",
          "reg:ks_referral",
          "reg:named_contact",
          "reg:not_monitored"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In preliminary, unpublished national figures, time from symptoms to treatment averages 155 days in Finland versus 107 days in Sweden and 67 days in Denmark—with 56 days of patient delay, 41 days in primary care, and 58 days in specialist care—and the Health Care Act sets no legal maximum time for a cancer suspicion.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "mot:total_fi",
          "mot:total_se",
          "mot:total_dk",
          "mot:patient",
          "mot:primary",
          "mot:specialist",
          "law:no_max"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "how_sure_are_we": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "Public registry data show 12-month treatment types, but county shares are crude, stage at diagnosis is often missing, and public data lack primary care, referral, and waiting-time timestamps.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
        "q:7885b0974f",
        "bs:coverage:Primary_care_occupational_health",
        "bs:coverage:Referral",
        "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "County shares are crude—unadjusted for age or stage because stage at diagnosis is frequently missing—and while national age-adjusted curative reference values exist in Kuva 16 (digitised from a figure at ±0.5 percentage points: 26.7% for men, 26.9% for women), Keski-Suomi's crude 27.2% (95% CI 23.9–30.7; n=173/637) already includes the national 27.0% (4009/14873).",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:curative:Keski_Suomen_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:curative",
          "k16:curative:men:national",
          "k16:curative:women:national",
          "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
          "q:7885b0974f"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Keski-Suomi's crude share with no treatment record within 12 months—mixing patients without treatment and unrecorded treatment—is 24.5% (95% CI 21.3–28.0; n=156/637), whose 95% confidence interval includes the national 27.5% (4089/14873); as an inference, not a finding, this is consistent with relatively complete treatment recording, while a journal article on about 90% HILMO concordance covers diagnoses only.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:no_treatment_record:Keski_Suomen_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:no_treatment_record",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start",
          "lit:hilmo_90"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Public report data do not measure symptom onset, referral dates, or when treatment started; outpatient primary care visits are not included in the report's data and occupational health is not mentioned, imaging appears only indirectly as the diagnostic basis in approximately 20% of cases, and specialist visits (93.6% nationally within 12 months) lack county breakdowns or dates.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:Symptoms",
          "bs:coverage:Primary_care_occupational_health",
          "q:323de0d90d",
          "bs:coverage:Referral",
          "bs:coverage:Imaging",
          "q:5eb155decc",
          "bs:coverage:First_specialist_visit",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "what_to_do_first": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "The team recommends reporting access times using THL guidance 21/2016 definitions with handover alerts, standardising referrals with a named diagnostic contact, and publishing county recording completeness.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "rec:1",
        "rec:2",
        "rec:3",
        "thl:21_2016"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "The team recommends reporting access times using THL guidance 21/2016 definitions and flagging stalled handovers, since Keski-Suomi's regional pathway document lacks referral time limits and monitoring data, while the roadmap plans pathway target times by 2026–2028 and the Filha programme's diagnostics recommendation with time limits is due before the 2030 mid-term evaluation.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:1",
          "thl:21_2016",
          "q:24169121a4",
          "reg:ks_referral",
          "reg:not_monitored",
          "q:4e702a20fe",
          "q:def306014c",
          "q:432c0e51d6",
          "q:614febebf2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The team recommends a standard referral template, a rule to refer persistent symptoms after a normal X-ray to a pulmonologist, and a named diagnostic contact—absent from regional pathway documents—supported by mentor insight that weak referrals get lower urgency ratings and roadmap plans for referral criteria and coordinator guidance in 2026–2028 (adopted in 2029–2031).",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:2",
          "mentor:kaisa_referral",
          "reg:named_contact",
          "q:556431a0c2",
          "q:37bb4c3b38",
          "q:c61439b30f",
          "q:fc81032a80",
          "q:abcbb06ae3",
          "q:050ee09ebe"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The team recommends publishing county recording completeness for stage, drug treatment, and MDT coding—reading Keski-Suomi's crude 3.8% (95% CI 2.5–5.5; n=24/637) recorded MDT share, whose 95% confidence interval excludes the national 6.0% (893/14873), as a recording gap—while a national quality registry targeting 90% coverage including stage is planned alongside the Cancer Registry.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:3",
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Keski_Suomen_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:mdt_recorded",
          "bs:coverage:MDT",
          "q:950a2f797b",
          "q:4c7a01d84c",
          "q:f07a34a300",
          "q:4a856bd695"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
